      "id": 10984,
      "name": "chainsawrabbit",
      "username": "chainsawrabbit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chainsawrabbit/{size}/2310_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-15T18:10:18.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Played my first skirmish last night with my wife. &nbsp;She used Beacon &amp; Ambsucade vs. Ra &amp; Tachyon.</p>\n<p>Holy crap, Tachyon can move. &nbsp;The raw stats really don't do it justice.</p>\n<p>Regardless, my wife came up with an interesting combo that raised a few questions. &nbsp;She had <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Cloaking Device</span> and <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Rigged Explosives</span> in play.</p>\n<p>On her turn, she used an action to spew trap tokens all over the map, mainly surrounding my heroes. &nbsp;Good lord, there are a lot of those bloody things.</p>\n<p>Then, in her <span class=\"bbcode-b\">To Be Continued…</span> phase, Ambuscade vanished off the map.</p>\n<p>The question is, <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Cloaking Device</span> explicitly says \"Ambuscade cannot take actions or activate abilities.\" &nbsp;Because of this, can his trap tokens still trigger when he isn't on the map, since it's dependent on the target and not on anything Ambuscade has to do? &nbsp;We played it that, because the tokens are already on the map and are hazard spaces, the traps are treated as a terrain feature and not a character-controlled effect.</p>\n<p>I just wanted to double check with a playtester, or someone who's better at interpreting these things than I am.</p>\n<p>Thanks in advance.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:11.329Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
